EFG 2 R "Fey et al. (1996), 6-move game: Centipede game" { "Player 1" "Player 2" }
"A constant-sum centipede game with 6 moves: the two players' payoffs sum to 3.20 at every terminal node. Players alternate, Player 1 first; at each move the mover chooses TAKE, ending the game, or PASS. This game was transcribed from Gambit's earlier example file and has not been checked against the paper."

p "" 1 1 "(1,1)" { "TAKE" "PASS" } 0
t "" 1 "Outcome 1" { 1.60, 1.60 }
p "" 2 1 "(2,1)" { "TAKE" "PASS" } 0
t "" 2 "Outcome 2" { 1.20, 2.00 }
p "" 1 2 "(1,2)" { "TAKE" "PASS" } 0
t "" 3 "Outcome 3" { 2.30, .90 }
p "" 2 2 "(2,2)" { "TAKE" "PASS" } 0
t "" 4 "Outcome 4" { .68, 2.52 }
p "" 1 3 "(1,3)" { "TAKE" "PASS" } 0
t "" 5 "Outcome 5" { 2.69, .51 }
p "" 2 3 "(2,3)" { "TAKE" "PASS" } 0
t "" 6 "Outcome 6" { .38, 2.82 }
t "" 7 "Outcome 7" { 2.92, .28 }
